===========================================================
  OSCILLATOR STAGE (Ultra‑Low‑Power Relaxation Oscillator)
===========================================================

Use ONE unbuffered inverter as the oscillator:

            +VDD
              |
              |
             [R]  100 kΩ – 1 MΩ
              |
              +-----------------------------+
              |                             |
              |                         +---+---+
              |                         | INV1  |
              |                         | (osc) |
              |                         +---+---+
              |                             |
              +-------------[C]-------------+
                            10 nF – 100 nF

Oscillator frequency approx:
    f ≈ 1 / (1.4 · R · C)

Examples:
    R = 100 kΩ, C = 10 nF → ~700 Hz
    R = 1 MΩ,   C = 10 nF → ~70 Hz

===========================================================
  OUTPUT BUFFER (Drive the Stylus Tip)
===========================================================

Paralleling 3–4 remaining inverters increases output strength:

                 +---+    +---+    +---+
Osc Out -------->|INV2|-->|INV3|-->|INV4|----+
                 +---+    +---+    +---+    |
                                               |
                                               |
                                        [ METAL CORE ]
                                        (runs entire length
                                         of stylus body)

===========================================================
  TIP ASSEMBLY
===========================================================

METAL CORE
   |
   +----> Covered by:
           - Conductive rubber tip  (best)
           - OR very thin plastic cone (works if thin)

This becomes the ACTIVE electrode touching the screen.

===========================================================
  BACK ELECTRODE (Pseudo‑Ground Plate)
===========================================================

Solar− (GND) ------------------------------+
                                           |
                                           |
                                   [ LARGE METAL PLATE ]
                                   (inside stylus body,
                                    acts as reference)

===========================================================
  FULL ELECTRICAL FLOW SUMMARY
===========================================================

Solar panel → reservoir capacitor → CD4069UB oscillator → 
buffered output → metal core → conductive rubber/plastic tip →
capacitive screen

Back electrode tied to Solar− provides the return reference.

===========================================================
  NOTES
===========================================================

• Requires bright indoor light or sunlight.
• Works on many capacitive screens but not guaranteed universal.
• No hand contact required — fully self‑powered & self‑referenced.
• Entire circuit fits inside a normal stylus barrel.
• Solar panel can be mounted externally like the “China Solar” style.

